INFO  [Claude Code] Excellent! The solution is complete. Let me provide a final summary:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ## Summary
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I've successfully resolved the two Diffblue Cover issues related to `PubSubConfig` test generation. Here's what was done:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Problem
INFO  [Claude Code] Both issues (Issue 1 and Issue 2) stemmed from the same root cause: When Diffblue Cover tried to generate tests for `PubSubConfig.positionPublisher()` and `PubSubConfig.tradePublisher()` methods, it attempted to use `@MockBean` to mock a generic `Publisher` bean. However, since `PubSubConfig` declares two beans of the same raw type `Publisher` (but with different generic parameters - `Publisher<Position>` and `Publisher<Trade>`), Spring couldn't determine which bean to mock, causing this error:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ```
INFO  [Claude Code] java.lang.IllegalStateException: Unable to register mock bean finos.traderx.messaging.Publisher<?>
INFO  [Claude Code] expected a single matching bean to replace but found [positionPublisher, tradePublisher]
INFO  [Claude Code] ```
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Solution
INFO  [Claude Code] I updated the existing `PubSubConfigDiffblueBase` class at:
INFO  [Claude Code] - `trade-processor/src/test/java/finos/traderx/tradeprocessor/PubSubConfigDiffblueBase.java`
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The base class now:
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. Uses `@ContextConfiguration` to load both `PubSubConfig` and a custom `TestConfig`
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. Provides `@Primary` stub implementations for all three beans:
INFO  [Claude Code]    - `Publisher<Position> positionPublisher()`
INFO  [Claude Code]    - `Publisher<Trade> tradePublisher()`
INFO  [Claude Code]    - `Subscriber<TradeOrder> tradeFeedHandler()`
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. Supplies the required `trade.feed.address` property via `@TestPropertySource`
INFO  [Claude Code] 4. Prevents Diffblue from using `@MockBean` by providing concrete beans
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Files Modified
INFO  [Claude Code] - `trade-processor/src/test/java/finos/traderx/tradeprocessor/PubSubConfigDiffblueBase.java` - Updated with Subscriber bean and better documentation
INFO  [Claude Code] - `compile-tests.sh` - Updated to mention both base classes
INFO  [Claude Code] - Created `PUBSUBCONFIG_FIX_UPDATED.md` - Comprehensive documentation of the fix
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Next Steps
INFO  [Claude Code] As you mentioned, you'll need to run:
INFO  [Claude Code] ```bash
INFO  [Claude Code] ./compile-tests.sh
INFO  [Claude Code] ```
INFO  [Claude Code] or
INFO  [Claude Code] ```bash
INFO  [Claude Code] mvn install -DskipTests
INFO  [Claude Code] ```
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] This will compile the base class so that Diffblue Cover can detect and use it when generating tests. After compilation, when you run Diffblue Cover again, it should automatically:
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. Detect the `PubSubConfigDiffblueBase` class (following the naming convention)
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. Generate tests that extend this base class
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. Successfully initialize the Spring context without ambiguity errors
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The issues should then be resolved and Diffblue will be able to generate tests for the `PubSubConfig` methods.
